      "mechanism": "JasperGold counterexample 24 cycles from reset, engine L, no abstraction (cover c_HOST_001, a write beat accepted, reached at cycle 1). wb_port.sv: wr_ack_r <= wb_beat & wb_we_i (the write acknowledge, one cycle after the beat) and assign wb_ack_o = wr_ack_r | rd_ack with rd_ack = rsp_valid. A read response arriving the cycle after a write beat is accepted gives one wb_ack_o pulse for two completions; the host counts one acknowledge, waits for the other forever (a pipelined master) or mis-attributes the read data to the write (a classic one). Any legal host reaches it: issue a read, then present a write beat the cycle before the read data returns. Not seen in simulation on 2026-10-28 only because no sequence placed a write beat on that cycle (243 pipelined beats on path_07). SIMULATION WITNESS (2026-10-29, path_23_host_ack_collision, ack_collision.py): a read to an open row and a write beat accepted 41 cycles later (gap d = 40) -- the write acknowledge and the read response fall in the same cycle at t = 35.37 us; a_HOST_001 fires once, every request and response is conserved, and the host handshake stage counts 1 of 79 beats never acknowledged: the one ack pulse the two completions shared. [found on drop 99f72da45a32; awaiting formal re-prove on e5ec723f495e]",
